; A commodity named "and", "div", "else", "false", "if", "not", "or" or
; "true" must be quoted in an amount, where a bare word like these is
; read as part of a value expression.  Ledger must keep the quotes when
; it prints such a commodity, or it cannot read its own output back.  A
; price directive names its commodity outside of any amount, so there the
; word needs no quotes (#3321).

P 2025/01/01 true $2.00

2025/01/01 Test
    Assets:A                                10 "and"
    Assets:B                               -10 "and"

test print
2025/01/01 Test
    Assets:A                                10 "and"
    Assets:B
end test

test pricedb
P 2025/01/01 00:00:00 "true" $2.00
end test
